{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++0x code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++0x code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<cstdint>\n#include<iostream>\n#include<vector>\n#include<cmath>\n\nint64_t nb_digits(int64_t n) {\n  if (n == 0) return 1;\n  n = n < 0 ? -n : n;\n  int64_t digits = 0;\n  do {\n    ++digits;\n    n /= 10;\n  } while (n);\n  return digits;\n}\n\nint64_t ones(int64_t n) {\n  int64_t res = 0;\n  while (n--) res = 10*res + 1;\n  return res;\n}\n\nint64_t aux2(int64_t n) {\n  if (n == 0) return 0;\n  n = n < 0 ? -n : n;\n  int64_t d = nb_digits(n);\n  return d + aux2(n-ones(d));\n}\n\nint64_t aux(int64_t n, int64_t sign, int64_t acc, int64_t max, std::vector<int> &already_in) {\n  if (acc >= max) return max;\n  if (n == 0) return acc;\n  if (n < 0) { n = -n; sign = -sign; }\n  int64_t d = nb_digits(n);\n  int64_t ones_d = ones(d);\n  int64_t res1 = max, res2 = max;\n\n  if (0 <= already_in[d]*sign && -10 < already_in[d] && already_in[d] < 10) {\n    already_in[d] += sign;\n    res1 = aux(n-ones_d, sign, acc+d, max, already_in);\n    already_in[d] -= sign;\n  }\n  if (0 <= already_in[d+1]*sign && -10 < already_in[d+1] && already_in[d+1] < 10) {\n    already_in[d+1] += sign;\n    res2 = aux(n-10*ones_d-1, sign, acc+d+1, res1, already_in);\n    already_in[d+1] -= sign;\n  }\n  return res1 < res2 ? res1 : res2;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  int64_t n;\n  std::cin >> n;\n  std::vector<int> already_in(20, 0);\n  std::cout << aux(n, 1, 0, aux2(n), already_in) << std::endl;\n  return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef nb_digits(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    n = abs(n)\n    digits = 0\n    while n > 0:\n        digits += 1\n        n //= 10\n    return digits\n\ndef ones(n):\n    res = 0\n    for _ in range(n):\n        res = 10 * res + 1\n    return res\n\ndef aux2(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    n = abs(n)\n    d = nb_digits(n)\n    return d + aux2(n - ones(d))\n\ndef aux(n, sign, acc, max_val, already_in):\n    if acc >= max_val:\n        return max_val\n    if n == 0:\n        return acc\n    if n < 0:\n        n = abs(n)\n        sign = -sign\n    d = nb_digits(n)\n    ones_d = ones(d)\n    res1 = max_val\n    res2 = max_val\n\n    # Check for d-digit option\n    if 0 <= already_in[d] * sign and -10 < already_in[d] < 10:\n        already_in[d] += sign\n        res1 = aux(n - ones_d, sign, acc + d, max_val, already_in)\n        already_in[d] -= sign\n\n    # Check for (d+1)-digit option\n    if 0 <= already_in[d + 1] * sign and -10 < already_in[d + 1] < 10:\n        already_in[d + 1] += sign\n        res2 = aux(n - 10 * ones_d - 1, sign, acc + d + 1, res1, already_in)\n        already_in[d + 1] -= sign\n\n    return res1 if res1 < res2 else res2\n\ndef main():\n    n = int(sys.stdin.readline().strip())\n    already_in = [0] * 20\n    result = aux(n, 1, 0, aux2(n), already_in)\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012015574611723423, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -0.632622480392456, 